        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Francine McDougall, Whitney Sloan, Everlife, Marley Shelton, Marla Sokoloff, Mena Suvari, James Marsden, Melissa George\n- Products: Go Figure, Cow Belles, Sugar & Spice, Go Figure soundtrack\n- Companies: Disney Channel, Walt Disney Records\n\nFacts:\n- In 2001, Francine McDougall directed the American teen crime comedy film Sugar & Spice, which starred Marley Shelton, Marla Sokoloff, Mena Suvari, James Marsden, and Melissa George.\n- In 2005, Go Figure was released as a Disney Channel Original Movie.\n- In 2005, Francine McDougall directed the Disney Channel Original Movie Go Figure.\n- On June 7, Walt Disney Records released the Go Figure soundtrack, featuring the title track by Everlife and a music video.\n- In 2006, Francine McDougall directed the Disney Channel Original Movie Cow Belles.\n- Whitney Adela Sloan, born on 21 August 1988 in London, is a British-born actress best known for playing Hollywood Henderson in the Disney Channel Original Movie Go Figure.",
